WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Two speech bubbles, one labelled
North, one labelled South.

2
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.440
Both say the same word: bath.

3
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.490
Listen.

4
00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.860
In the North it's a short vowel.

5
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.080
In the South it stretches out, long.

6
00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:17.700
But write it down, and
both bubbles just say bath.

7
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.130
The spelling hides the difference.

8
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.700
So how do you write down a sound?

9
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.410
In this mission, you'll
ask what a sound is,

10
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.050
if it isn't a letter.

11
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.280
Bat and pat differ by just one.

12
00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:36.080
You'll ask why bath, laugh and aunt can
spell the same vowel three different ways.

13
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.030
And you'll test some ways
of writing a sound down,

14
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.010
and decide which one a linguist can trust.

15
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:45.500
Your mission: work out
how to write down a sound.
